infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Fixing the NOT IN NULL trap: NOT NULL constraint vs NOT EXISTS
  desc The deciding question — can you forbid NULL at the schema, or must you fix existing queries in place?
  compares
    - label NOT NULL constraint
      children
        - label Strongest fix — bug impossible by construction
          desc Forbids the NULL that collapses NOT IN to UNKNOWN
        - label Protects every query at once
          desc Removes the root cause for the whole column, not one query
        - label Requires a schema change and migration
          desc Backfill and validate existing rows before the constraint
        - label Only when the column can truly never be NULL
          desc Not an option where NULL is a legitimate value
    - label NOT EXISTS
      children
        - label Safest drop-in replacement for NOT IN
          desc Fixes an existing query with no schema change
        - label NULL-safe — tests row existence, not value equality
          desc A NULL in the subquery can never force UNKNOWN
        - label Usually plans better as an anti-join
          desc Often a faster plan than NOT IN as well
        - label Must be applied per query
          desc Every NOT IN call site has to be rewritten
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
